# Files and directories excluded from the published WordPress.org package.
#
# The zip carries what runs and nothing else. Build tooling, manifests and
# configuration stay behind: none of it is read at runtime, and a customer
# opening the plugin folder should find the plugin.
#
# Plugin Guideline 4 wants the source behind minified build/ output to be
# reachable. readme.txt's "Source code" section names the public repository
# holding assets/ and the build configuration, which is what satisfies it.
#
# vendor/ has to come from `composer install --no-dev`. .distignore cannot strip
# development dependencies itself: they are transitive, so the names nobody
# lists by hand outnumber the ones anybody would. bin/package.mjs refuses to
# build without it, reading composer's own record of what it installed.

/.git
/.github
/.claude
/.gitignore
/.distignore
/.editorconfig
/.eslintignore
/.eslintrc
/.eslintrc.js
/.eslintrc.json
/.prettierrc
/.prettierrc.js
/.stylelintrc
/.stylelintrc.json

/node_modules
/tests
/docs
/coverage

/phpunit.xml
/phpunit.xml.dist
# Excluding phpunit.xml.dist and not this one shipped the integration config to
# every customer. Glob what belongs to the suite rather than listing variants.
/phpunit-integration.xml.dist
/phpunit*.xml
/phpunit*.xml.dist
/.phpunit.result.cache
/.phpunit.cache
/composer.lock
/package-lock.json

# End-to-end suite and everything that drives it.
/tests-e2e
/test-results
/playwright.config.ts
/playwright-report
/TESTING.md
/bin/install-wp-tests.sh

# Local development environment, not the plugin.
/.idea
/.vscode
/.wp-env.json
/.wp-env.override.json
# Tracked and currently clean, but a tracked .npmrc is usually a registry
# credential and this is the wrong place to find out.
/.npmrc

/README.md
/ROADMAP.md
# Screenshots and banners for the directory listing. The deploy action reads
# them from the checkout and publishes them to SVN assets/; copying them into
# the payload ships 740 KB of marketing art to every install, and into trunk.
/.wordpress-org
# .gitignore keeps these out of the repo; this keeps them out of the zip.
# They live on disk, so being untracked hides them from git and from nothing
# else: without these lines the build would ship the QA findings and the
# internal working notes to every customer.
/CLAUDE.md
/qa
# Generated codebase analysis. Gitignored, which is exactly why it reached a
# customer zip: git never sees it, and this list is the only thing that stops
# it. 19 MB of internal notes about our own source.
/graphify-out

# Our own build and release scripts. They run from a checkout, never from an
# install, and package.mjs shipping inside its own output is just odd.
/bin
# Build configuration. Runtime loads the compiled build/ directly, so neither is
# read once the plugin is installed, and the repository readme.txt names is
# where anyone rebuilding it should be looking anyway.
/package.json
/webpack.config.js

# composer.json is deliberately absent from this list. A payload carrying a
# vendor/ and no manifest is the one thing in it that cannot say where those
# six packages came from, and Plugin Check calls that out by name.

# Strauss copies these into vendor-prefixed/ and the plugin loads only that copy.
# The originals stay behind in vendor/ because they are direct requirements, so
# without this the zip carries two of every PDF library: dead weight, and a
# second unprefixed copy an add-on could autoload by accident.
/vendor/dompdf
/vendor/masterminds
/vendor/sabberworm

/vendor/phpunit
/vendor/bin

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.zip
*.log
*.map

# Vendor test suites. Strauss copies dependencies whole, so their own tests and
# fixtures come with them, and none of it runs.
/vendor/vendor-prefixed/dompdf/dompdf/tests
/vendor/vendor-prefixed/dompdf/php-font-lib/tests
/vendor/vendor-prefixed/dompdf/php-svg-lib/tests
/vendor/vendor-prefixed/masterminds/html5/test
/vendor/vendor-prefixed/sabberworm/php-css-parser/tests
# Queryable is ours, so it was easy to miss: Strauss copies it whole like any
# other dependency, tests and lockfile included.
/vendor/vendor-prefixed/dono/queryable/tests
/vendor/vendor-prefixed/dono/queryable/composer.lock
/vendor/vendor-prefixed/dono/queryable/phpunit.xml.dist

/.cache
